review:
+Интересная механика игры;
+Есть бонусы подстегивающие играть дальше;
-Как только вольетесь в игру и начнете побеждать, вас обязательно выкинет и переподключиться не сможете. Проверьте целостность файлов, якобы неисправно античит-приложения. При том, что после проверки покажет, что все файлы целые, вас в любом случае выкинет. Либо перед запуском игры делайте проверку целостности файлов каждый раз, что бы снизить процент выбрасывания из игры.

I originally picked up and played Palworld around its Early Access launch. While I never reached the late game back then, I could definitely see the potential the game had.

Coming back for 1.0, I can confidently say I enjoyed it. There were changes throughout Early Access that occasionally put me off, particularly as the game evolved alongside the ongoing legal situation surrounding it, but the end result still feels like a breath of fresh air for the monster-catching/survival/base-building genre.

Whether you're coming from Pokémon or you simply enjoy survival games, there's a lot here to like. In particular, after so many Pokémon generations where new mechanics can sometimes feel more like incremental or seasonal additions than fundamental changes, Palworld is refreshingly willing to experiment with the formula.

Is the game without faults? Absolutely not. There are several issues I encountered during Early Access that I hoped would be resolved by 1.0, but unfortunately are still present:
[list]
[*] No search function in the Pal Box; filtering is there but it's not enough once you have a big collection;
[*] On dedicated servers, Base Pals can & will eventually starve themselves as they seem to fail to eat; whether it's a pathfinding issue when no players are present or something else I don't know;
[*] AI pathfinding/targeting is still fairly basic;
[*] Base automation, or what exists of it, is somewhat lacking and requires a fair bit of babysitting to work reliably;
[*] Some balancing changes could be in order - mid/late game crafting and construction takes unholy amounts of grinding and very long processing. Going into research & sending your Pals to expeditions help, but it's still too long for solo/offline players who cannot afford to leave their PC AFK. While the game allows you to adjust these settings, they should be adjusted for SP experiences by default I feel.
[/list]

Despite these problems, I think PocketPair was able to bring this in as a breath of fresh air in the Pokemon-like universe with about 80% of the vision they had - since some of the infomercial GIFs and whatnot are definitely misleading from what the game actually offers - but despite that, I overall had fun.

Recommended!
